  "rte": {
    "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
    "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "kristian.bocage@stryker.com",
    "text": "<p><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Strength</span></span><br>\nStructurally intact matrix offers strength during tissue regeneration and allows for high tensile strength to augment soft tissues during the healing process.<sup>1,2</sup></p>\n<p><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\">Performance</span></span><br>\nAn acellular, porous, collagen matrix allows for early cellular repopulation, remodeling, and revascularization. Evidence of cellular infiltration, new blood vessel vascularization, and host tissue remodeling in a preclinical animal model.<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p><span class=\"fontsize-1-25em\"><span class=\"futura-bold\">Ease of use</span></span><br>\nProLayer Xenograft does not require rehydration or rinsing and can be implanted directly from packaging. The xenograft can also be implanted in either direction facing downward.<sup>1</sup></p>\n",
    "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Feb 21 2022 15:49:51 GMT+0000",
    "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
    "textIsRich": "true"
  },
